## gpu-probe: zero-copy consumer proof attempt (lavapipe)
# HONESTY: this sandbox caps a single mmap at ~126 GiB; llvmpipe's LLVM JIT
# reserves ~94 TB for shader codegen -> vkCreateShaderModule returns
# OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY. The ALLOCATION leg (real Vulkan HOST_VISIBLE device
# memory, persistent map, live fan-out publishes through it) is PROVEN
# below; the DISPATCH leg (compute shader validating live ring words) is
# CI-gated (gpu-native shard, standard kernels allow the reservation).
```
gpu-probe: vkCreateShaderModule rc=-1 (OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY — shader JIT address-space reservation refused by this kernel/sandbox)
gpu-probe: backend=vulkan device='llvmpipe (LLVM 19.1.7, 256 bits)' payload=256 slots=4 frames=1000
gpu-probe: allocation-leg PROVEN — vulkan device memory, persistent map, 100 live frames published through it (latestSeq=100, publishes=100)
gpu-probe: dispatch-leg UNAVAILABLE in this environment (shader JIT address-space reservation) — the full dispatch proof runs in the CI gpu-native shard
exit: 4 (4 = allocation proven, dispatch env-limited)
